Patch 0007. You can now work what the last two patches produce, and get the engine
live without leaving the Codespace.

/admin/pipeline

- Every purchased engagement with its state, and a Release button on anything sitting
  in draft. Release stays the one deliberate human act in the flow; the button exists
  so it is not a curl.
- Every hall anyone has run through the qualifier: as found, after the ladder, what
  bound it, how complete the intake was, and who they are.
- Four counters that matter: waiting on you, engagements, committed revenue, halls
  qualified.

WHAT ACTUALLY BINDS

The section that compounds. Across every hall that has been through the engine: the
distribution of binding constraints, and the median tap-off rating, busway ampacity,
plant supply temperature and contracted headroom behind it.

Anyone competent can rebuild the physics from public sources. Nobody else is
accumulating what binds in real European halls, hall by hall, with the numbers that
produced it. At a few dozen halls that is a sales argument. At a few hundred it is a
paper nobody can write without us. `summariseQualifications` is deliberately a pure
function over the rows so it stays testable and cheap as the table grows.

fetchDeliverables selects the document columns only to derive has_document, and drops
the bodies before they leave the data layer — a list view has no business shipping
megabytes of HTML to render a row.

DEPLOY

`scripts/deploy-engine.sh`: installs flyctl if missing (the Codespace has no `fly`),
signs in, creates the app, generates the API key, deploys, waits for health, and prints
the two variables to set on Vercel. One command from a bare shell.

111 Python tests pass. tsc, next lint and next build clean.

